From 7bec1ca6f52f1c10834b3a3aa7c5570feeeb4ef6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:52:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pilotd: local mode

[local] in pilotd.toml runs the standard backend on the phone: the LLM is
llama.cpp's llama-server on this machine with a short prompt of its own,
and LocalJev stands in for Jev. The phone's parsers take what they do
without a model; apps and actions (the two-stage tool routing) are ranked
by a small embedding model plus shared words, so the model sees only the
tools that fit; web.search is a service on the phone. No relay, no Reef
licence, no keys; replies are stamped as processed on the device, and
answers say they were written on the phone.

The system prompt no longer carries the time: it moved to the turn, so a
model server's prompt cache keeps the prompt.
